From: Perry Raskin <perryraskin@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sio: block A7 activation pending shared DMA ownership

Exact owner firmware model resets peripheral DMA controls before READY.
No audio-only boot opt-in may bypass that unresolved shared ownership.
Other SoCs are unchanged. A7 sources remain buildable for bring-up.

--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
@@ -1023,6 +1023,13 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPERM,
 				     "Experimental J86 SIO boot disabled or wrong board/page size\n");
 
+	/* Firmware startup resets 32 peripheral DMA controls before READY.
+	 * An audio-only mapping lease cannot establish ownership of those blocks.
+	 * Keep A7 compile-only until a shared-controller handoff is implemented. */
+	if (hw->legacy_a7)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EOPNOTSUPP,
+				     "J86 shared-peripheral firmware handoff is not implemented\n");
+
 	sio = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*sio), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!sio)
 		return -ENOMEM;
